# Normalise line endings in the repository.
#
# Without this, every file's line endings depend on each developer's local
# `core.autocrlf`. A shell script committed from a Windows checkout with CRLF
# fails on Linux at the shebang itself — `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` is read as a
# request for an interpreter literally named "bash\r", and the error
# ("No such file or directory") points at the file rather than the line ending,
# which makes it a genuinely confusing failure.
#
# `text=auto` stores text as LF in the repo and lets Git hand Windows checkouts
# CRLF; the explicit `eol=lf` entries below are for files that must be LF *in
# the working tree too*, because something other than Git reads them.

* text=auto

# ── Must be LF even in a Windows working tree ────────────────────────────────
# Executed by a shell, directly or inside a container.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.dockerfile    text eol=lf
.env.example    text eol=lf

# Read by Fluent; keep byte-identical across platforms so locale diffs stay
# reviewable rather than showing every line as changed.
*.ftl           text eol=lf

# Note: `.ps1` needs no rule of its own. PowerShell parses LF and CRLF equally
# on every platform, and `pwsh` runs on Linux and macOS too, so pinning it to
# CRLF would only force Windows line endings onto checkouts that have no use for
# them. `text=auto` above already gives Windows working trees CRLF.

# ── Binary: never touch, never diff as text ──────────────────────────────────
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gif           binary
*.webp          binary
*.ico           binary
*.woff          binary
*.woff2         binary
*.ttf           binary
*.eot           binary
*.zip           binary
*.fpkg          binary
*.pdf           binary

# Built asset bundles: committed on purpose (other developers must not need
# Node to run the app), but reviewing them line-by-line is noise.
frontend/static/js/ferum-widgets.iife.js  -diff
frontend/static/js/*.min.js               -diff
frontend/static/css/*.min.css             -diff
